course: dictionary
lesson: 5563
title: Words for food and seeds
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are names for foods you may never have eaten. You can still work out their meaning from the clues around them. «We cooked a pot of lentil soup and ate it with warm bread.» Cooked, soup and ate tell you that a lentil is a food you can cook.
explain: Check your guess by swapping your meaning into the sentence. If your meaning still makes sense, you are probably right. Clues can also come from the words next to the hard word, such as «red lentils» or «a handful of lentils».
explain: Look for the name of a group too. A lentil is a small round flat seed, and it is also a pulse, part of the bean and pea family. Knowing the family helps you guess what a lentil is like.
fact: A lentil is a small round flat seed.
fact: Lentils can be brown, green, red or yellow, and they grow in pods.
fact: Lentils are a pulse, part of the bean and pea family.
fact: Lentils are cooked and eaten, often in soups and stews, such as «lentil soup».
fact: Lentils are a cheap source of protein and fibre, so they are important in food for people who do not eat meat.
exercise: «Beans, lentils, nuts, tofu and eggs give plenty of protein to people who do not eat meat.» What is a lentil in this sentence? | A type of shoe | A kind of pen | *A food that gives protein | A large wild animal
exercise: «We cooked a pot of red lentils with onions and carrots.» What are lentils? | Hard metal tools | Pieces of dried leaves | *Small seeds that are cooked and eaten | Small stones from a river bed
exercise: Which family is the lentil part of? | Cat and dog family | *Bean and pea family | Ant and bee family | Rose and daisy family
test: «Lentils grow in pods.» Where does a lentil grow? | Inside a bowl of soup | *In a pod | Under the sea | On the roof of a house
test: Ella says a lentil is a large, heavy stone. What is the correct idea? | It is a bright light | It is a kind of cloud | *It is a small round flat seed | It is a large, hard stone
exam: Which of these is a lentil, and what clue helps you know? | A wooden bead from a necklace | *A small seed that is cooked in soup, as in «lentil soup» | A flat stone from a pond | A grain of sand from a beach
